<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Inventory's public face: the only thing another module is allowed to know
       about this one. Requests, responses and an interface — no logic, no
       infrastructure, and deliberately no reference to Inventory itself.

       Zero PackageReference items, and zero ProjectReference items, both on
       purpose. A consumer takes a dependency on this assembly and nothing
       else, so referencing it cannot drag EF Core, Redis or Inventory's domain
       into a module that has no business seeing them.

       This is also what makes the extraction story in DECISIONS 001 concrete.
       When Inventory becomes its own service, this assembly is what stays
       behind in the monolith as the client contract: Orders keeps compiling
       against the same interface and only the registered implementation
       changes, from an in-process call to an HTTP one. -->

</Project>
